# Shikues_78L33 — component wrapper: local KiCad symbol + footprint, LCSC pinned
# in properties (feeds the JLC BOM/CPL fields).
#
# NEW PART (2026-07-26, cnc-expansion capture). Fixed 3.3V linear regulator, SOT-89
# (tabbed, decent thermal handling for its size), 100mA. Stock listing confirmed at LCSC
# C2999140 (checked 2026-07-26); the 78L33/L78L33 family (this is a same-pinout, same-spec
# rebrand of ST's L78L33) is a ubiquitous, long-established part, effectively always
# available across many manufacturers. Input up to 30V abs max (datasheet, 2026-07-26) —
# safely covers AMP_RAIL_ISO's full 15-24V range (B2415S-2WR3 default / VFD_24V bypass).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: the isolator (Chipanalog_CA_IS3720HG) needs a 2.5-5.5V logic supply on
# its isolated side (VDDB/GNDB) — a different, much lower rail than AMP_RAIL_ISO's 15-24V
# analog supply for the LM358. A simple R+zener shunt was sized first but the dissipation
# across AMP_RAIL_ISO's full 15-24V swing (at the few-mA load the isolators draw) needed an
# uncomfortably large resistor power rating for an 0603/0805 part; this 3-pin LDO handles
# the same job with a normal SOT-89 dissipation budget and tighter regulation. Derives
# V_ISO_LOGIC (~3.3V) from AMP_RAIL_ISO, referenced to AGND_ISO — entirely within the
# isolated domain, does not cross the isolation barrier.
OUT = io("OUT", Net, optional = True)
GND = io("GND", Net, optional = True)
IN = io("IN", Net, optional = True)

Component(
    name = "Shikues_78L33",
    footprint = File("Shikues_78L33/SOT-89-3_L4.5-W2.5-P1.50-LS4.2-BR.kicad_mod"),
    symbol = Symbol("Shikues_78L33/78L33.kicad_sym"),
    prefix = "U",
    part = Part(mpn = "78L33", manufacturer = "Shikues"),
    properties = {"LCSC": "C2999140", "MPN": "78L33"},
    pins = {
        "OUT": OUT,
        "GND": GND,
        "IN": IN,
    },
)
